1
00:00:07,480 --> 00:00:10,847
The baby's invisible and it's your fault.

2
00:00:11,080 --> 00:00:14,801
My fault! Whose box has she got?

3
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:18,048
-How did she get it? -Oh, I don't know.

4
00:00:18,239 --> 00:00:19,888
I didn't see her.

5
00:00:22,120 --> 00:00:25,010
And what about your box? You haven't got it.

6
00:00:26,359 --> 00:00:30,647
So now we can't be invisible. And that's your fault.

7
00:00:31,320 --> 00:00:33,321
I'm sorry, Corvax.

8
00:00:34,439 --> 00:00:37,806
But I got you out of the river. I got you out.

9
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:40,081
Don't argue, Thimbo!

10
00:00:40,479 --> 00:00:44,040
-I'm not arguing. -Yes, you are.

11
00:00:44,399 --> 00:00:46,799
-No, I'm not. -Yes, you are.

12
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:49,001
-No, I'm not. -Yes, you are.

13
00:00:50,840 --> 00:00:54,322
Stop it! We must find the baby.

14
00:00:56,920 --> 00:00:58,365
Look outside!

15
00:01:05,359 --> 00:01:09,330
Muzzy, is that the house? Is that the right one?

16
00:01:09,519 --> 00:01:10,680
Perhaps.

17
00:01:11,200 --> 00:01:12,804
I'm not sure.

18
00:01:13,040 --> 00:01:17,328
My black box isn't working. So I'm not sure.

19
00:01:19,840 --> 00:01:23,082
Well, I'm sure. That is the right house.

20
00:01:23,519 --> 00:01:26,362
It's got a blue door and three windows.

21
00:01:26,840 --> 00:01:28,251
Come on!

22
00:01:30,400 --> 00:01:32,606
What are we going to do?

23
00:01:33,239 --> 00:01:36,082
And what's the King going to do?

24
00:01:37,439 --> 00:01:38,679
Aha!

25
00:01:38,879 --> 00:01:42,041
He's going to have a surprise.

26
00:01:44,920 --> 00:01:48,641
Be careful! Corvax is there.

27
00:01:48,840 --> 00:01:52,764
-It's dangerous. -Don't worry! It's safe here.

28
00:01:53,159 --> 00:01:56,641
It isn't safe. And I'm frightened.

29
00:01:56,879 --> 00:01:58,562
Well, I'm not frightened.

30
00:01:59,359 --> 00:02:01,680
I'm going to go inside. Now!

31
00:02:02,599 --> 00:02:04,600
I'm coming Corvax!

32
00:02:16,240 --> 00:02:18,446
-Be careful! -Careful?

33
00:02:18,680 --> 00:02:21,160
I'm going to get Corvax.

34
00:02:26,840 --> 00:02:27,807
Corvax!

35
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:29,889
This is the King!

36
00:02:30,080 --> 00:02:32,730
Oh! Your Majesty!

37
00:02:32,960 --> 00:02:35,531
What do you want, your Majesty?

38
00:02:35,719 --> 00:02:37,323
Why are you here?

39
00:02:37,560 --> 00:02:39,243
We want Amanda.

40
00:02:39,439 --> 00:02:41,520
The little princess?

41
00:02:41,759 --> 00:02:43,760
She isn't here.

42
00:02:44,439 --> 00:02:47,169
She's in the Palace. There's no one here.

43
00:02:48,360 --> 00:02:52,046
Well, there's only me, and Thimbo.

44
00:02:52,879 --> 00:02:57,042
Thimbo, I've got a clever idea.

45
00:02:57,319 --> 00:02:58,730
They can come in.

46
00:02:59,759 --> 00:03:00,884
What?

47
00:03:01,599 --> 00:03:03,727
Bob and the King

48
00:03:03,919 --> 00:03:05,842
and that huge,

49
00:03:06,039 --> 00:03:09,168
enormous green monster?

50
00:03:09,360 --> 00:03:10,565
Yes.

51
00:03:10,960 --> 00:03:14,282
Amanda's invisible. They can't see her.

52
00:03:15,560 --> 00:03:17,528
They can hear her.

53
00:03:17,800 --> 00:03:19,881
I'm going to turn the radio on.

54
00:03:20,919 --> 00:03:22,443
Loud!

55
00:03:22,639 --> 00:03:25,482
No one can hear the baby now.

56
00:03:30,840 --> 00:03:33,365
Your Majesty,

57
00:03:33,680 --> 00:03:35,841
Princess Sylvia,

58
00:03:36,159 --> 00:03:38,605
your Majesty,

59
00:03:39,039 --> 00:03:42,885
Bob! Please come inside, everyone!

60
00:03:43,960 --> 00:03:46,485
Stop that awful noise!

61
00:03:51,919 --> 00:03:53,364
What are you doing here?

62
00:03:53,599 --> 00:03:55,760
I'm on holiday.

63
00:03:56,599 --> 00:04:00,240
I always come here for my holiday.

64
00:04:00,520 --> 00:04:01,931
You were at the party.

65
00:04:02,120 --> 00:04:04,009
And someone took Amanda.

66
00:04:04,280 --> 00:04:06,930
We went away before the party.

67
00:04:09,520 --> 00:04:11,409
When did we come here?

68
00:04:11,879 --> 00:04:14,962
Today is the third.

69
00:04:15,680 --> 00:04:18,126
-We came... -We came here yesterday.

70
00:04:18,319 --> 00:04:19,559
Quiet, Thimbo!

71
00:04:20,040 --> 00:04:23,567
We came here the day before.

72
00:04:24,160 --> 00:04:27,881
We came here on the first.

73
00:04:30,680 --> 00:04:33,330
Norman, what's the date today?

74
00:04:33,720 --> 00:04:34,925
Let's look.

75
00:04:42,199 --> 00:04:44,645
Today's the third.

76
00:04:44,920 --> 00:04:47,650
The second was yesterday.

77
00:04:48,480 --> 00:04:52,087
And the first was the day before that.

78
00:04:53,199 --> 00:04:55,679
Today's the third.

79
00:04:56,720 --> 00:04:58,848
Tomorrow's the fourth.

80
00:05:00,160 --> 00:05:04,483
And the fifth is the day after that.

81
00:05:05,480 --> 00:05:08,210
And after that come the sixth

82
00:05:09,600 --> 00:05:11,329
and the seventh.

83
00:05:12,480 --> 00:05:15,689
Then the eighth, ninth, tenth

84
00:05:17,160 --> 00:05:19,208
and eleventh.

85
00:05:25,120 --> 00:05:28,761
All the way to the thirty-first day.

86
00:05:29,439 --> 00:05:33,841
And that's my holiday! Hooray!

87
00:05:38,240 --> 00:05:40,970
Today's the third.

88
00:05:41,160 --> 00:05:43,970
And tomorrow's the fourth.

89
00:05:45,160 --> 00:05:48,527
-And the day after that... -Corvax, stop that!

90
00:05:48,959 --> 00:05:51,007
-Someone took Amanda. -Ow!

91
00:05:51,240 --> 00:05:54,005
-What's the matter? -Something bit me.

92
00:05:54,439 --> 00:05:56,203
Something bit you?

93
00:05:57,160 --> 00:05:59,731
Someone bit you.

94
00:06:00,160 --> 00:06:03,447
-Amanda. -But she isn't here.

95
00:06:03,639 --> 00:06:04,764
Oh dear!

96
00:06:04,959 --> 00:06:07,724
We've got terrible flies in here.

97
00:06:07,959 --> 00:06:09,404
It was a fly.

98
00:06:09,600 --> 00:06:10,840
Look! There it goes!

99
00:06:11,639 --> 00:06:14,244
Stop that noise, Corvax.

100
00:06:14,720 --> 00:06:17,724
Now, listen. Listen everyone.

101
00:06:25,759 --> 00:06:27,124
Did you hear that?

102
00:06:27,319 --> 00:06:29,447
She's here, in this room.

103
00:06:30,240 --> 00:06:31,651
Mummy!

104
00:06:32,360 --> 00:06:34,124
Daddy!

105
00:06:36,399 --> 00:06:39,766
Where is she, Corvax? You know.

106
00:06:40,160 --> 00:06:42,083
And your little friend.

107
00:06:42,360 --> 00:06:46,251
-Where is she? -I don't know.

108
00:06:46,519 --> 00:06:47,884
Yes, he does.

109
00:06:48,279 --> 00:06:51,646
He knows. He took the baby.

110
00:06:51,879 --> 00:06:53,209
Shut up, Thimbo!

111
00:06:53,399 --> 00:06:55,048
He's got a little box.

112
00:06:55,240 --> 00:06:59,767
You push a button and you're invisible.

113
00:07:00,279 --> 00:07:04,125
The baby's got the box and now she's invisible.

114
00:07:05,959 --> 00:07:08,007
Muzzy! You take those two!

115
00:07:08,639 --> 00:07:10,403
Now, everyone!

116
00:07:10,600 --> 00:07:13,410
Look on the floor! Look for Amanda!

117
00:07:17,480 --> 00:07:19,323
-Ah! I've got her. -Here she is!

118
00:07:20,079 --> 00:07:22,400
-No, she isn't. -Over here! This way!

119
00:07:22,600 --> 00:07:24,170
-Quick! -No!

120
00:07:25,800 --> 00:07:28,121
I'm sure she's here.

121
00:07:28,959 --> 00:07:30,802
There's something here.

122
00:07:31,319 --> 00:07:33,447
Ow! Yes!

123
00:07:33,759 --> 00:07:35,602
Here she is!

124
00:07:39,319 --> 00:07:42,129
Corvax! We can't see her.

125
00:07:42,319 --> 00:07:44,208
Do something, Corvax!

126
00:07:44,439 --> 00:07:46,964
I can't do anything.

127
00:07:47,160 --> 00:07:49,685
The baby's got my box.

128
00:07:50,279 --> 00:07:53,521
Corvax has lots of other things here.

129
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:56,206
-What do you mean? -Look!

130
00:07:56,560 --> 00:07:58,528
Press that switch.

131
00:07:58,920 --> 00:08:00,524
Turn that handle.

132
00:08:04,959 --> 00:08:06,848
My goodness.

133
00:08:07,079 --> 00:08:09,160
Look at that!

134
00:08:25,040 --> 00:08:28,362
Stop it! You mustn't do that.

135
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:31,081
One of these...

136
00:08:31,439 --> 00:08:35,080
with one of these.

137
00:08:36,120 --> 00:08:38,441
This to this.

138
00:08:39,919 --> 00:08:42,604
These in here.

139
00:08:44,960 --> 00:08:47,201
That's it! There!

140
00:08:54,639 --> 00:08:56,960
Amanda! Amanda!

141
00:08:58,519 --> 00:09:00,408
Hello, Mummy!

142
00:09:01,879 --> 00:09:03,960
Hello, Daddy!

143
00:09:05,440 --> 00:09:08,842
Whoopee! Darling! Wonderful! Hooray!

144
00:09:24,840 --> 00:09:26,523
What am I going to do?

145
00:09:26,720 --> 00:09:29,724
-You were stupid, stupid, stupid! -Where am I going to go?

146
00:09:29,919 --> 00:09:32,923
-I was clever, clever, clever. -What are they going to do?

147
00:09:33,120 --> 00:09:36,407
-But you were stupid, stupid, -Why did I do it?

148
00:09:36,679 --> 00:09:38,362
Why? Why? Why?

149
00:09:38,879 --> 00:09:41,450
It's all your fault!

150
00:09:48,879 --> 00:09:51,007
This is our new clock.

151
00:09:51,519 --> 00:09:53,840
We finished it yesterday.

152
00:09:54,720 --> 00:09:57,485
Three cheers for the new clock!

153
00:09:57,960 --> 00:10:00,008
Hooray! Hooray! Hooray!

154
00:10:00,720 --> 00:10:02,961
This is our new clock.

155
00:10:03,600 --> 00:10:05,886
Listen to its sound!

156
00:10:06,759 --> 00:10:08,965
That was our new clock.

157
00:10:09,919 --> 00:10:12,160
It's going round and round.

158
00:10:12,919 --> 00:10:15,080
This is our new clock.

159
00:10:15,519 --> 00:10:17,520
We're going to go inside.

160
00:10:19,080 --> 00:10:21,003
Now we're inside the clock.

161
00:10:21,399 --> 00:10:24,164
It's time to say goodbye.

162
00:10:24,639 --> 00:10:25,639
<i>Goodbye ,r</i>

163
00:10:26,039 --> 00:10:27,039
<i>Goodbye ,r</i>

164
00:10:27,679 --> 00:10:28,919
<i>Goodbye ,r</i>

165
00:10:39,080 --> 00:10:40,570
Goodbye!

166
00:10:43,679 --> 00:10:45,044
Goodbye!

167
00:10:49,120 --> 00:10:50,690
Goodbye!

168
00:10:54,600 --> 00:10:56,011
Goodbye!

